{
  "request": {
    "method": "GET",
    "path": "/v1/formats/spark/1/schema.json"
  },
  "response": {
    "status": 200,
    "headers": {
      "Content-Type": "application/schema+json"
    },
    "body": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "$id": "https://akl-db/formats/spark/1/schema.json",
      "title": "spark/1 payload",
      "description": "The common format (design/layout-db/22-spark-spec.md): cmini's positions, the magic-rules authoring shape from design/magic-rules/02-schema.md, plus a raw-rule escape hatch. There is NO board field (design/layout-db/26-no-board.md): a record says where its keys sit and which finger presses each, never what physical board it is drawn on -- the board is the reader's own choice (the site's rowstag/ortho comparison view, the bot's engine context), so 23-geometry.md's one-word `board` is gone along with its object predecessor. 21-formats.md D10 dropped the free-form `x` field; 23-geometry.md dropped the `TB` finger (its section 4.2: a thumb key's label IS its hand), and its own duplicate-characters follow-up replaced the char-keyed `keys` map (plus a separate `free` array) with ONE array of positions -- `char` optional (absent = free), and the SAME char may appear on more than one entry. Single-code-point-ness, cross-field agreement and referential checks (no two entries share (row, col), a magic-named char has at most one entry, etc.) are NOT expressible here -- they live in formats/spark/1/index.ts's validate().",
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
        "keys"
      ],
      "properties": {
        "keys": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/key"
          }
        },
        "magic": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/magic"
        },
        "alts": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/alt"
          }
        },
        "combos": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/combo"
          }
        }
      },
      "$defs": {
        "key": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "row",
            "col",
            "finger"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "char": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "row": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": -1,
              "maximum": 4
            },
            "col": {
              "type": "integer",
              "minimum": 0
            },
            "finger": {
              "enum": [
                "LP",
                "LR",
                "LM",
                "LI",
                "RI",
                "RM",
                "RR",
                "RP",
                "LT",
                "RT"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        "magic": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "magic_keys": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/magicKey"
              }
            },
            "chiral_keys": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/chiralKey"
              }
            },
            "adaptive_swaps": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/adaptiveSwap"
              }
            },
            "rules": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/rawRule"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "magicKey": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "key"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "key": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "default": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/magicDefault"
            },
            "rules": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/magicKeyRule"
              }
            },
            "except": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "magicDefault": {
          "description": "design/layout-db/24-spark-wire-review.md finding 6, round 2's resolution item 1: a `kind`-discriminated tagged union, not bare strings -- absent means none (there is no 'none' tag).",
          "oneOf": [
            {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": [
                "kind"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "kind": {
                  "const": "repeat"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "object",
              "additionalProperties": false,
              "required": [
                "kind",
                "char"
              ],
              "properties": {
                "kind": {
                  "const": "char"
                },
                "char": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "chiralValue": {
          "description": "design/layout-db/24-spark-wire-review.md finding 6, round 2's resolution item F: the SAME kind-tagged union as magicDefault -- a literal character is `{kind:\"char\",char}`, never a bare string; the 'repeat previous' sentinel is `{kind:\"repeat\"}`.",
          "$ref": "#/$defs/magicDefault"
        },
        "magicKeyRule": {
          "description": "design/layout-db/27-magic-emit.md: after the n-gram `after`, the key emits `emit` -- the lowered row is `after+key -> after+emit`. A magic key never rewrites its context (a row that would is a raw `rules[]` entry). `emit` replaced the old `output` (which repeated the context) on purpose: new meaning, new name.",
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "after",
            "emit"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "after": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "emit": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            }
          }
        },
        "chiralKey": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "key"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "key": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "same": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/chiralValue"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ]
            },
            "opposite": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/chiralValue"
                },
                {
                  "type": "null"
                }
              ]
            },
            "except": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "adaptiveSwap": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "trigger",
            "swap"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "trigger": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "swap": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "minItems": 2,
              "maxItems": 2
            }
          }
        },
        "rawRule": {
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "inputs",
            "output"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "inputs": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 2
            },
            "output": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            },
            "type": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "note": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "alt": {
          "description": "design/alts/07-format.md: an alternate fingering for one NGRAM. `ngram` is an array of 2 or 3 items, each a string of exactly one code point or null (the wildcard: any key; allowed only as the middle item of a 3-item ngram; a literal \"_\" is just the underscore key). `fingers` is an array of the same length: the finger code (same enum as key.finger) that types that position's character in this alt, null at exactly the ngram's wildcard. A code equal to the key's own finger means no move and is valid. Deliberately loose here (items have minLength 1 only -- code points, not UTF-16 units, are what count; no length link between the two arrays): every rule that depends on the layout or on the ngram lives, with path-naming messages, in index.ts's validateAlts.",
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "ngram",
            "fingers"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "ngram": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 2,
              "maxItems": 3,
              "items": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            "fingers": {
              "type": "array",
              "minItems": 2,
              "maxItems": 3,
              "items": {
                "oneOf": [
                  {
                    "enum": [
                      "LP",
                      "LR",
                      "LM",
                      "LI",
                      "RI",
                      "RM",
                      "RR",
                      "RP",
                      "LT",
                      "RT"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "combo": {
          "description": "design/alts/07-format.md: a two-key chord. Both members are the layout's own chars (index.ts's validate()); `output` need not be. `output` is 1-2 CODE POINTS, checked in index.ts (no maxLength here, same reason alt.ngram has none).",
          "type": "object",
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "required": [
            "keys",
            "output"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "keys": {
              "type": "array",
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "minItems": 2,
              "maxItems": 2
            },
            "output": {
              "type": "string",
              "minLength": 1
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
